WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
- It's time to make some meatballs

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:04.728
'cause what's more Italian
than some meatballs.

00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:05.561
(meatball whooshing)

00:00:05.561 --> 00:00:07.300
Hey, everyone, I'm Chef Joe Sasto.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.740
And today, I'm going to be turning

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.860
one of these mystery
ingredients into pasta.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.680
Well, we have some crazy options here.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.272
Let's find out what I'm making today.

00:00:15.272 --> 00:00:18.400
(wheel clacking)

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.630
All right, a Chipotle burrito.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.450
I'm okay with that one,
that's not too hard.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.100
It's not the easiest option on here.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.040
Let's just get started.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.184
I think first things first, we
need to order some Chipotle.

00:00:27.184 --> 00:00:28.860
(doorbell ringing)

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.330
And we have our Chipotle.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.550
So we got the whole thing.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.750
Obviously, some chips,
salsas, we'll include those.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.650
I have some ideas, the ideas are flowing.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.100
I know how to work those
into the mix, right.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.080
We got a healthy portion
of crema. Thank goodness.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.110
'Cause that actually is my favorite part,

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:50.000
and wow, a very tiny burrito.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.620
Am I crazy? Didn't they used
to be much bigger than this?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.170
Let's open this up.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.244
We'll give it a little, a
quick bite, a taste test.

00:00:57.244 --> 00:00:59.070
(upbeat music)

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.670
Okay, we've got steak, beans and rice.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.050
I have all these on the side.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:06.030
I'll use everything. Just to keep it fair.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.250
This is gonna be good. I know what to do.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:10.563
We got this, let's make some pasta.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.040
First things first, we
need our pasta dough.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.280
Now I've never done this before.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.140
Obviously, I've made quite
a bit of pasta dough,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:23.140
but my instincts tell me to
use the rice in the dough.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.860
So we're gonna go our
burrito rice into here.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.960
I'm gonna to give it
a little bit of flour,

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.363
just to get it started.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.060
I'm using double zero and semolina.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.920
A little of this, a little of that.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.980
(food processor whirring)

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.733
I got just a little bit of
room temperature water here.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.240
All right, that is the
beginning of our pasta dough.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.430
I am gonna use the rest of this flour,

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.690
and the rest of this flour.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:58.330
And of course, you know,
a little bit of salt.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.680
It goes a long way, making
everything taste better.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.063
Slowly adding in some water.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.797
Voila! Huh? How bout that?

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.810
Who would've thought you can turn

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.440
Chipotle burrito rice into pasta dough.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.273
Time to knead,

00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:17.130
I'm gonna take just a
little bit of flour here,

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:19.530
just to make sure we're not gonna stick.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:20.740
I already could tell right now,

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.780
I'm gonna use this to make some cavatelli.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.130
I don't think that's
ever been done before.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:26.780
First time ever things are happening here,

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:27.700
and you're watching it.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.020
You're part of it.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.230
Pasta dough is done.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:31.940
Let's get this wrapped up

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.390
and break down the rest of that burrito

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.993
for the rest of our pasta.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.610
So I need to incorporate the
burrito tortilla here some way.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.760
So I'm just gonna go ahead

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.930
and cut this into some thin strips.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.850
So butter is hot, nice, and sizzling.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.620
We'll come in with our tortilla strips.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:59.160
A little pinch of salt
and our chipotle powder

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.410
for our Chipotle burrito.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.080
Chipotle, smoked dried jalapenos

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.640
for anyone out there that was wondering.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.340
Most chilies have two names,

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:10.230
a name when they're fresh and
a name when they're dried.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.400
Interestingly enough.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.980
So I'm just going to
let my crumble rumble.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.860
I'm going to throw this into the oven,

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.010
let it get nice and crispy.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.953
And then it's time to make some meatballs

00:03:18.953 --> 00:03:22.680
because what's more Italian
then some meatballs.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.440
So I have my steak here
from my Chipotle burrito.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.440
We'll start with a little bit
of olive oil, some onions.

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.770
We'll start with a little sofrito here,

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.500
diced onions, some chopped garlic.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.100
We'll sweat this down.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.430
Onions and garlic cooked down.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:42.520
Nice, soft and translucent.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:45.510
And we'll go in with all that steak.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.750
I got a little bit of smoked paprika here.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.960
Let's just toss this all together.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.373
Toss, toss, toss. That
looks and smells awesome.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.430
So I'm going to let
this cool in the fridge.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:03:59.980
I'm going to grab more tortilla chips

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.870
and then we're going to
turn it all into meatballs.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.680
I want to grind these
down into bread crumbs.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.513
Except it's not bread,

00:04:06.513 --> 00:04:09.450
they're going to be tortilla
chip crumbs for our meatballs.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.403
I'm probably only going to
use, eh, we'll use that many.

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:21.453
All right, so steak now
into our tortilla crumbs.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.380
Into here instead of ground beef.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:29.700
Now we need, uh let's see, an egg.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.803
This is going to be our binder,
hold everything together.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.460
We're on our way.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.130
Look at that. That is meatballish.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.033
Taste test. Make sure
we like our seasoning.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.430
Gloves on. Time to form some meatballs.

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.060
I'm going to use a little scoop here,

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.210
just to keep things nice and consistent.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.900
Now I'm just going to come through here,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.430
make these all nice and pretty.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.910
The true testament of this is at the end,

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:05.780
when we're tasting it.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.080
If they can't tell that we
started with a Chipotle burrito,

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.840
I think we accomplished our mission.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.160
A little more olive oil into a hot pan.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.840
There's no raw meat in here.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.160
So really I just want to
crisp them up on the outside.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.820
Get a little bit of color.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.070
We're just going to let these guys

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.700
finish cooking all the way through,

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.400
and then we're cooking some pasta.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.413
For a sauce,

00:05:27.413 --> 00:05:30.260
I'm going to incorporate the pinto beans

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:33.000
that I had picked out of
my burrito from earlier.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.560
I'm also going to supplement that

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:37.010
with a little bit of vegetables over here.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:40.190
Starting with a hot saute pan,

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:44.970
we're going to go in with a
couple of tablespoons of butter.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.740
Butter makes things taste better.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.350
Melt that down, bring it together.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:52.490
We have some diced onion.
We've got some diced carrot.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:57.270
Ready to incorporate our beans.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:00.130
And then we have this pico to use, right?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.230
So we'll do a little bit
of that tomato in there.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.800
Toss that all together to combine.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:09.520
And then I do want to kind
of cook this down together,

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.550
make this all become one.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.940
This is a beef stock.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.850
And so I'm just going to cover everything

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:17.160
with a little bit of stock.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.770
We'll bring this up to a simmer,

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.120
reduce it just a little bit,

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.450
and then we're going to
throw it all into the blender

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.670
till it's nice and smooth.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:28.670
So our bean ragu has
reduced to about half here.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.600
Now I just want to blend it all together,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:35.451
and we'll have a nice,
smooth and creamy bean sugo.

00:06:35.451 --> 00:06:38.520
(blender whirring)

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.980
Let's give it a little
taste test for approval.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.823
We're nice and smooth creamy.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:48.190
Oh! No one's going to know
this is a Chipotle burrito.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.290
I don't even know it's a Chipotle burrito.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.123
I'm going to see this up

00:06:51.123 --> 00:06:54.183
with just a little squirt of lime juice.

00:06:55.843 --> 00:06:57.260
And it's time to roll out some pasta.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.570
I'm going to just going
to divide this into,

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.293
let's call it sixths.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.473
I know math is hard.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:06.780
Then those will be ready.

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:11.690
I'm going to come in here and
take each strip and roll it.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:13.090
Might need the spray bottle.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.780
There we go. Now we're rolling.

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:18.930
I'm Italian. I'm allowed
to do this, right?

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:21.380
So those are all done.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:23.480
I got all of my snakes finished.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:28.170
Going to take my flour now and
just dust that over the top.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:32.520
So snakes are together. Then
we can come in with our cutter.

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.643
I like to go in half and go down the row.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:42.280
Pasta magic happening
right before your eyes.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:47.280
That's not it. Now we have
all of our cavatelli, almost.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:53.280
Then you come in here and I'm
gonna use a cavarola board,

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.790
just to put a little bit of
texture and that notorious

00:07:56.790 --> 00:08:00.290
little cup on each piece of pasta.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.610
And then we're on to the moment of truth,

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:03.500
we've all been waiting for.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.013
Time to cook this and
bring it all together.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.890
So we got all of our rice,
Chipotle cavatelli noodles.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:16.520
One of a kind, maybe the one and only time

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.730
this will ever be done.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:21.310
Perfect, lid back on.
So where you're boiling.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:24.290
So noodles are floating here.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.490
We'll give it a little-.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:29.260
Much more fluffy then
I would have imagined.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.520
Really nice texture on those.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:33.720
That's pleasant. I liked that.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.190
What a fun surprise, huh?

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.513
Our noodles are done.
Into our meatball pan.

00:08:39.970 --> 00:08:41.620
A little bit of that pasta water.

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:45.030
Always our friends, some starchy water.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.780
We call that the white gold.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.180
I have our bean sugo from earlier.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:53.143
Will go one nice spoonful of that.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.313
And now, hear that sound?

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.010
Sound of good pasta my friends, huh?

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:07.563
We'll go pasta down
first. In our bean ragu.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.103
Let's go crema. Crema is next.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:14.090
Oh my, look at that.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.493
Next, our meatballs.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:23.200
Next, a little bit of our
cilantro for freshness.

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:28.460
We have our crispy
crumbly tortilla strips.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.620
What a beautiful looking bowl of pasta,

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:33.080
made from a Chipotle burrito.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.170
Now we just got to bring
in our taste tester.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.480
Alex, welcome.
- I'm back!

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:38.120
- You're back.
- For more.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.840
- I have another pasta here for you.

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.690
- Oh!
- Smell Test.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.273
- Smells great. Kind of smells like beans.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.010
- You're good. Yes.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.460
Yes. There you're on the right track.

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.400
I like this.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.450
- Okay, gotta get some
pasta. Gotta get some sauce.

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.620
- You're a good bite
builder. That's a good bite.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:57.840
- This tastes like Mexican food

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.640
- Yes. You're on the right track.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:00.473
It's fast food.

00:10:00.473 --> 00:10:02.150
- Like a burrito bowl?

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:07.150
- Close. I mean it's a
burrito from Chipotle.

00:10:07.335 --> 00:10:08.210
- Oh (bleep)

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:10.725
- Yes.
- You're a star.

00:10:10.725 --> 00:10:11.766
You're so creative

00:10:11.766 --> 00:10:12.599
- Thank you for watching.

00:10:12.599 --> 00:10:14.650
I want to know, let me
know in the comments,

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.110
what I should make into pasta next.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:17.990
- Can I eat it?

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:20.425
- And we'll have Alex here forever to try.

00:10:20.425 --> 00:10:21.588
- (Indistinct)

00:10:21.588 --> 00:10:22.763
- The ultimate judge.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:25.100
- I'm okay with being a judge.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.844
- Oh, yes.

00:10:26.844 --> 00:10:29.927
(upbeat jazz music)

